1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,244
Most journals in Miftah write themselves:
posting a

2
00:00:03,244 --> 00:00:06,083
contract, clearing a cheque, closing a
month.

3
00:00:06,083 --> 00:00:08,921
The journal voucher is for everything
else.

4
00:00:08,921 --> 00:00:11,354
As the Accountant, open Journal Voucher.

5
00:00:11,354 --> 00:00:16,220
Every entry in the books is listed here,
manual and automatic, with

6
00:00:16,220 --> 00:00:21,086
its document type: TCO for a tenancy
contract, PDR for a cheque

7
00:00:21,086 --> 00:00:25,547
received, CIL for month-end recognition,
and JV for a manual journal.

8
00:00:25,547 --> 00:00:26,764
Filter on JV.

9
00:00:26,764 --> 00:00:31,224
In April, the cash from Arjun Mehta's
returned cheque was banked.

10
00:00:31,224 --> 00:00:34,063
JV-26/1 debits the Emirates Islamic
account 14,000

11
00:00:34,063 --> 00:00:36,496
and credits the Cash Account 14,000.

12
00:00:36,496 --> 00:00:39,740
The money moved from the cash box to

13
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:42,578
the bank, so no tenant balance changes.

14
00:00:42,578 --> 00:00:43,795
Now a correction.

15
00:00:43,795 --> 00:00:47,850
A 600 deep-cleaning bill was booked to
Repairs and Maintenance.

16
00:00:47,850 --> 00:00:49,472
Select New Journal Voucher.

17
00:00:49,472 --> 00:00:54,338
Enter the date, 30 September, after the
locked period; the property, Palm

18
00:00:54,338 --> 00:00:58,799
Ridge Residences; and a narration that
tells the next reader why.

19
00:00:58,799 --> 00:01:00,421
Debit Cleaning Services 600.

20
00:01:00,421 --> 00:01:03,259
Until the other side is entered, Miftah

21
00:01:03,259 --> 00:01:06,098
shows the difference and will not post.

22
00:01:06,098 --> 00:01:08,125
Credit Repairs and Maintenance 600.

23
00:01:08,125 --> 00:01:11,369
Debits now equal credits, so Post is
enabled.

24
00:01:11,369 --> 00:01:12,586
JV-26/3 is posted.

25
00:01:12,586 --> 00:01:15,830
Now suppose the bill had already been
moved.

26
00:01:15,830 --> 00:01:19,074
You never edit or delete a posted journal.

27
00:01:19,074 --> 00:01:23,129
Select Reverse, keep 30 September, give a
reason, and confirm.

28
00:01:23,129 --> 00:01:27,995
Miftah posts JV-26/4, the mirror image,
linked as the reversal of JV-26/3.

29
00:01:27,995 --> 00:01:30,834
The original stays in the ledger, marked

30
00:01:30,834 --> 00:01:33,672
Reversed, and the two net to zero.

31
00:01:33,672 --> 00:01:36,511
Journals the system writes, such as a

32
00:01:36,511 --> 00:01:39,349
contract's TCO, have no Reverse button
here.

33
00:01:39,349 --> 00:01:42,593
They are corrected from their own
document, so

34
00:01:42,593 --> 00:01:45,432
the contract and its ledger never
disagree.
